Content and usage data includes information that is automatically generated or collected while using the software. This
includes, for example:
* Connection and log data to ensure the technical security of the software;
* Identification and access data to enable access to the software;
* Information about the devices used, such as the type and version of the device and the version of the operating
system, in order to ensure correct display.
2. Content and Data
Content data includes information that users create or upload via the software, or that is generated during use. This
includes, for example:
* Text posts, images and media content (e.g. teaching materials, contributions in courses);
* Other documents uploaded by the user;
* Data you enter when creating prompts or in forms.
3. Student data
Student data includes information required for student administration. This includes, for example:
* name data, contact details, student ID number and other identification numbers;
* assignment to degree programs, faculties, and years/semesters of study;
* participation in events, courses, and groups;
* statistics on learning progress;
* information on medical certificates and compensatory measures.
4. Data for communication
Communication data includes information required for student administration. This includes, for example:
* Chat messages sent via the messaging function;
* Interactive content (e.g. surveys, polls);
* Camera and microphone data when participating in courses via video chat.
5. Examination and Assessment Data
Examination and test data are processed as part of examination management. The exams are created by administrators
or instructors and completed by learners. These data include, for example:
* General information about the exam (e.g. type of exam, exam process, instructor, assessment criteria, matriculation
number);
* Exam questions and content (e.g. questions, answers);
* Participation in exams (e.g. time of completion or submission);
* Exam results and assessments (e.g. grades, points, comments);
* Log data related to exams (e.g. access to exam questions).
6. Data of teaching staff
The data of teaching staff are processed for the organization of courses. These data include, for example:
* identification data;
* contact details;
* titles and qualifications as well as status group;
* information on course and room allocations;
* information on courses.

